WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.840
South Pole Squad

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.160
Penguinger!

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.160
South Pole Squad

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.050
Penguinger!

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.960
Wow...

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.100
So you're going to be on TV?

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.200
Yes!

00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.340
Yama Yama! Yama Arashi!
Producer Machikawa Koji

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.960
I would love for you 
to be on the show.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.010
What?!

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.230
You're going to be on 
Yama Arashi's show?!

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:07.850
Yes...

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.850
Well done!

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.740
You mean we'll be able 
to meet Yama Arashi?!

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:14.070
Um, uh... no...

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.750
We have to hurry and make 
an appointment at the salon!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:17.820
You're right.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.510
Um...

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.510
The nail salon, too!

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.740
Of course!

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.920
A-ra-shi!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.960
Shi!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.750
Wow, so you're going to 
be on it, too, Panda?

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.160
Yeah!

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:38.500
I'll throw living rooms across the country
 into a panic with my cuteness!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.890
You should be helping them relax.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.100
Your role was the evil emperor, 
right, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.600
Yeah, the dark hero.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.320
So wild.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.580
Do you want to be on it, 
too, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:59.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.170
So this is a TV station!

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:08.560
So excited!

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.250
So this is it...

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.850
The place that'll pay me just 
to eat and get into the hot springs.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.980
Please be quiet, Panda.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:20.600
Hello...

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.680
We're Yama Arashi.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.640
It's a pleasure to 
work with you today.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.310
The same goes for u—

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.940
Um, this isn't much, but...

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.730
Oh, you shouldn't have.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.660
We've received a present!

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.690
Thank you very much!

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.660
They're Toraya's Yama Arashi buns.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.190
Oh, from the famous Toraya.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.410
I've always wanted to try one.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.640
Thank you very much.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.630
Um...

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.130
Pardon me, but it's about time.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.670
This is the set.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.560
There's nothing there.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.210
I guess the TV station's 
hit hard times, too.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.250
Please be quiet!

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.060
Well, the background 
is completely CG.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.980
We're rolling in...

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.110
Five, four...

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.410
South Pole Squad

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.580
Penguinger!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.790
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.250
<i>So crisp and satisfying.</i>

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.520
<i>Polar Bear Soda now on sale!</i>

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.520
It's finally starting!

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.820
So exciting!

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.180
Yama Yama! 
Yama Arashi!

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.910
Yama Yama! Yama Arashi!

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.750
Arashi!

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.180
Arashi!

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.510
Now, for our next segment, 
we have us, Yama Arashi, and...

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.230
...the petting zoo's popular 
South Pole Squad Penguinger!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:07.570
Penguinger

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:07.570
South Pole Squad

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.570
South Pole Squad Penguinger!

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.910
<i>Are you ready?</i>

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.580
<i>We're going to take you</i>

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.500
<i>To the night-time savanna</i>

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.300
<i>We are nocturnal...</i>

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.040
We were totally just on TV!

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.220
Oh, how embarrassing.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.770
<i>Were you surprised?</i>

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.650
Wh-What's going on?

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.650
What the heck?! What's going on?

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.300
Stop it!

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.960
Arashi!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.750
Let us out of here!

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.610
Let us out!

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.510
And now the era of Yama Arashi 
has come to an end.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.310
It is now the era of traditional 
entertainment, comedic storytelling!

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.530
Thanks for the Full House

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.990
First Generation Emperor Penguin

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.170
And now another idiotic tale.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.250
<i>Hey, pour him another cup.</i>

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.530
What is this?

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:49.070
<i>Ah, landlord...</i>

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.450
The evil emperor

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.690
<i>Something good will happen at the tenement house very soon.</i>

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.140
hijacked the world's airwaves

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.100
and broadcasted "The Flower Viewing 
From the Tenement House."

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.970
<i>How do you know that?</i>

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.310
<i>The liquor leaves tell me so.</i>

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:58.810
Penguinger!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.560
South Pole Squad

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.560
Penguinger

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.940
Café
Shirokumaya

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.400
Hey! It's my scene next!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.990
Could I get another coffee, Pops?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:12.920
Sure thing.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.450
Pops, could I get four large 
servings of curry ice cream?

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:23.040
Our large servings are the real deal.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.500
Better make it two.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.410
I want my usual!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.290
A large serving of 
bamboo grass, right?

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.060
Everyone's here.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.750
I'm so cute.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:43.240
They reached an instantaneous max 
viewership of forty percent right there.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.650
Was that your whole scene, Panda?

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.390
Yeah.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.160
This is their secret base:
The Penguinger Room.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.670
The Evil Emperor kidnapped 
Yama Arashi.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.880
Your mission is to safely 
rescue Yama Arashi

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.400
and defeat the Emperor army.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.430
That is all.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.340
Penger!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.920
Spotted! That way!

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:24.020
There...

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:25.980
Penguinger Jet!

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:27.690
Go!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.170
Evil Emperor's Secret Base

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.130
Dang it!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.020
What are you planning to do with us?!

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:50.850
Let us go!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.590
You're... the Evil Emperor!

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:58.600
Rejoice.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.680
I'm going to turn your 
bodies into ones that can

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.980
only listen to comedic storytelling.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.020
S-Stop!

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.680
Wh-What's going on?

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:16.450
That's...

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.410
Gentooger!

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:28.240
Chinstrapger!

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.840
Adélienger!

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:35.620
South Pole Squad

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.020
Penguinger!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.900
Get them!

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:45.980
Let's go!

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.480
Penger!

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.880
Adélien Kick!

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.590
Gentoo Flipper!

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.490
Chinstrap Beam!

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.160
Give it up!

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.100
This way.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.300
Way...

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.540
Thank you, guys.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.170
Rescue complete.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:18.720
Thank you!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.050
Ah, crap.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:24.060
Curse you, Penguingers!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.500
The ruler of the South Pole, 
the Evil Emperor!

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.140
Why are you doing this?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.010
What a foolish question.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:35.750
It's because I am evil!

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.150
I hate those who are popular!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.910
Nothing will come from hatred!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.520
I'm going to take 
revenge on the world

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.540
that called my comedic 
storytelling boring!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.210
Get them!

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.190
Spiky Spiky!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.910
You can do it, Penguingers!

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:14.980
Gers!

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.250
You guys...

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.900
We have no other choice!

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:28.450
P-Penger...

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.740
Let's go! Penguinger Storm!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.290
Penger!

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:35.470
Spiky Spiky!

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.300
Here we go, Gentoo!

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:44.760
Yeah!

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.980
It's up to you, Adélie!

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.730
It turned into a fish dumpling!

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.000
Fish!

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.490
It's a super hot pot!

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:08.210
Spiky Spiky!

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.770
Curse you, Penguingers!

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:19.880
I'll let you live today.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.470
You'll pay for this!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.390
Pa pi pu pe po!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.060
Pen penguin!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.800
Thank you, Penguingers!

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:37.220
If something happens again...

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:38.880
...we'll come to your aid anytime.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:41.240
Because we're...

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:43.290
South Pole Squad

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.160
Penguinger!

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.270
And so peace was restored 
to the Earth again.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.640
You are true heroes.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.700
Thank you, Penguingers!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.810
Penguingers!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.320
Man, I'm totally cute.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:07.420
<i>And now, please listen to our 
song: Yama Arashi Tonight!</i>

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.220
Was your scene really needed?

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.160
We were on a lot!

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.310
Yeah.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:17.230
Mr. Rockhopper, your death scene 
at the end was fantastic!

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.660
Nah. You guys were super cool, too.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:23.110
Thanks for all your hard work!

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.490
What's the matter?

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.720
I had ad-libbed a whole bunch of puns,

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:36.050
I wonder why they were cut.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.690
South Pole Squad

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.500
Penguinger!

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.810
They're even more popular 
since the broadcast.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:52.500
The penguin cards sales 
have exploded, too.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.440
Delivery!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.150
What's this?

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.380
It seems to be a DVD.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:07.860
Who's it from?

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.450
Llama

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:09.610
Llama?!

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.370
Herbivore Squad

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.370
Llamaranger

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:19.050
Llamaranger?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.960
I wonder if it's a 
spin-off of Penguinger?

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.550
Llama Yellow!

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.130
Llama Blue!

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:26.720
Llama Red!

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.560
Herbivore Shquad

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.050
Llamaranger!

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:35.260
Erbivore Squad.... Herbivore Squad...

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:36.550
Hamaranger!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.440
Herbivore Squad...

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.890
He can't say it right...

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.000
<i>Herbivore Hentai!</i>

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.120
Let's pretend we never saw this...

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:55.410
Even More, What is Roasting!?

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.570
Even more...

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:55.410
What is roasting?!

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:16.550
Masaki!

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.340
Keep your hands moving!

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:20.900
R-Right!

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:25.860
Roasting <i>(baisen)</i>?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.990
Those are daffodils <i>(suisen)</i>!

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.910
That's a bison!

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.750
Ma-ma-ma-mahalo!

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.330
That's an anime song <i>(anison)</i>!

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.400
I said roasting!

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.080
R-o-a-s-ting!

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.690
Are you still not allowed to roast?

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.290
I've been able to practice with 
beans that we don't need...

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:49.800
But I haven't done it
 for real even once.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.460
Which probably means 
that in Master's eyes,

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.160
I still have a ways to go.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:16:01.040
Well, even when you're serious,
you look all flashy.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:06.590
You have such a cute face 
but a sharp tongue, Panda!

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.740
I know I'm cute!

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:15.320
Your ears have a 
noise-canceling function

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.080
that blocks out anything 
inconvenient to you, don't they?

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:18.580
Masaki,

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.540
try eating these.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.430
S-Sure.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.210
What do you think?

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.940
They have a coarse texture...

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.430
But when I bite into them,

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.650
the aroma of coffee fills my mouth

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.930
and I can really taste the flavor.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:38.210
Right?

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:40.490
It's a bit bitter and sour,

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.000
but it's rather delicious.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:45.440
Coffee beans that have 
been roasted properly

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.900
taste good even if you eat them.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.170
Just like Mr. Tree Kangaroo's.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.450
I want to be able to roast delicious 
beans like this someday.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:00.000
Hopefully you'll be able 
to roast properly soon.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.410
Yeah! I'll do my best!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:14.800
Nice to meet you, Miss Sasako.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.230
What is that?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.770
You don't know?

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.130
It's ventriloquism.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.380
Oh...

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.090
I'm currently apprenticing under 
Master Golden Snub-nosed Monkey

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:25.770
who I hit it off with at an 
izakaya... So I started...

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.730
Train... ing...

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.910
Tree Kangaroo Coffee

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:44.030
Your roasting technique 
is getting much better.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.210
Today I'm not using reject beans

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.470
so I'm going to treat everyone 
to some special Masaki coffee.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.850
Oh, really?

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.420
Here you go.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:00.520
It's delicious.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:04.190
It looks like you may 
have improved, Masaki.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.580
Really? Yes!

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:11.020
But I still want to drink 
something a bit more rich.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.100
Oh, really?

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.660
Masaki's coffee has bitterness,

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.950
but I think it's lacking richness.

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.160
<i>Richness?</i>

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:25.740
<i>If I pour it slower, 
shouldn't it be richer?</i>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.420
I have a delivery for 
Polar Bear's Café.

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.540
R-Right! I'll take it!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:38.230
You're so harsh, Mama Red Squirrel.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:43.280
Masaki's coffee tastes 
much better than before.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.560
And he's working so hard.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:49.560
He's also gotten much 
better at hand picking.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.870
Well...

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.890
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:03.410
What's the richness of coffee?

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.830
Richness?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:09.850
Mama Red Squirrel said 
I'm lacking richness.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:15.710
Yeah. Your face is lacking 
richness, Masaki.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:18.090
Such a venomous tongue.

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.870
Indeed... it... is...

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.160
Maybe that's enough, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.100
How are you pouring the coffee?

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.020
With a paper drip filter.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:36.350
Then it'll end up having a light 
flavor without much richness.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.140
What do you mean?

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:42.170
The flavor of coffee changes depending 
on the equipment you use.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:43.490
Really?!

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:45.100
To test things out,

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.810
let's compare different preparation 
methods with the same beans.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.670
First, a flannel filter.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.210
It's a milder taste than a paper drip.

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:00.130
Next, a coffee press.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:06.100
This is the most rich!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.310
I didn't know the taste 
could change so much...

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:11.590
It's the oil of the beans 
that determines the richness.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.480
Light

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.570
The more oil, the richer it becomes.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.310
Rich                                                    Light

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.420
So I guess the equipment 
used is important, too.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.290
I'm ba—

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.560
About Masaki...

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.560
Isn't it about time?

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:34.250
It's been over six months, hasn't it?

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:37.670
Masaki's working really hard.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.580
Let's allow Masaki to do some roasting.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.480
Why are you red squirrels 
bringing this up?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.620
That was my intention.

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:17.130
I was actually going to have him 
start helping me roast tomorrow.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.550
Oh, really?

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.470
Master!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:23.870
Masaki!

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:26.870
Really, Master?!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.220
Oh, you were here.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:34.890
I want you to be able to 
roast Tree Kangaroo coffee.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:40.200
<i>I'll be able to roast the 
same flavor as Master!</i>

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:44.700
I... I'll do my best!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.220
Congratulations, Masaki.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:58.480
I, Masaki, am training to be 
a master coffee roaster.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:05.340
I'm Penguin.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.100
I'm training to become...

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:12.230
a... ven... tril... oquist...

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.280
Mr. Penguin,

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.540
how long are you going to do that?

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.120
Tonight...

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:24.720
Until... morning...

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.810
Next Time

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:58.790
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:00.040
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:03.430
I wonder why they don't 
release a laundry detergent

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.040
that smells like wet laundry.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.840
Probably because they think it stinks.

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.830
So they have something like that now?

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:10.570
No, they don't.

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:12.720
You need to be concentrating 
when you're not talking, too.

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:14.260
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:14.460 --> 00:24:16.320
Please watch next week's 
Polar Bear's Café

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:19.050
from fifty meters away from your TV.

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:21.060
I don't think even 
Mr. Sankhon could see that.

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:21.770
Sloth's Trip
I Became a Doll
White Day

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:22.060
Sankhon?

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:23.110
One-khon, two-khon...

00:24:23.110 --> 00:24:24.220
Enjoy!
